---
/**
 * The five stages of /examples/, in reading order. Each stage is one row: a numbered
 * node on a rail, the stage link, and one line on what it covers. The whole row is a
 * click target for the stage link; stage 2 also links straight to its three recipes.
 * Plain HTML in reading order, styled by examples-learning.css (not-content, so the
 * theme's Markdown rules stay out).
 */
import './examples-learning.css';
---

<nav class="ex-learning not-content" aria-label="Examples learning path">
  <ol class="ex-learning-steps" role="list">
    <li class="ex-learning-step">
      <span class="ex-learning-num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
      <div class="ex-learning-card">
        <a class="ex-learning-title" href="#minimal-queue-and-worker">Run one job</a>
        <div class="ex-learning-body">
          <p class="ex-learning-note">Start with one queue and one worker in the same process.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="ex-learning-step">
      <span class="ex-learning-num" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
      <div class="ex-learning-card">
        <a class="ex-learning-title" href="#understand-the-job-lifecycle">Make failure predictable</a>
        <div class="ex-learning-body">
          <p class="ex-learning-note">Follow the lifecycle, then add retries, schedules, and idempotency.</p>
          <ul class="ex-learning-links" role="list" aria-label="Recipes in this stage">
            <li><a href="#retries-and-the-dead-letter-queue">Retries</a></li>
            <li><a href="#scheduled-and-repeating-jobs">Schedules</a></li>
            <li><a href="#deduplicate-jobs-with-jobid">Deduplication</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="ex-learning-step">
      <span class="ex-learning-num" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
      <div class="ex-learning-card">
        <a class="ex-learning-title" href="#choose-a-deployment-topology">Split into processes</a>
        <div class="ex-learning-body">
          <p class="ex-learning-note">Move to TCP, observe events, and shut workers down safely.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="ex-learning-step">
      <span class="ex-learning-num" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
      <div class="ex-learning-card">
        <a class="ex-learning-title" href="#workflow-automatic-rollback-on-failure">Orchestrate workflows</a>
        <div class="ex-learning-body">
          <p class="ex-learning-note">
            Coordinate compensation and human decisions after queue fundamentals are clear.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="ex-learning-step">
      <span class="ex-learning-num" aria-hidden="true">5</span>
      <div class="ex-learning-card">
        <a class="ex-learning-title" href="#end-to-end-example-projects">Scale to multiple brokers</a>
        <div class="ex-learning-body">
          <p class="ex-learning-note">Finish with the tested PostgreSQL topology and its engineering report.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>
</nav>
